From: Nik <sibnick@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] plat/kvm/x86: drop empty TLS program headers to prevent GRUB 2.12 overlap error

When an application has no thread-local storage data, the linker emits an empty
PT_LOAD program header at the same address as the subsequent data segment.
GNU GRUB 2.12 multiboot loader detects overlapping segments and aborts boot with:
    error: overlap detected.

Dropping tls PT_TLS and tls_load PT_LOAD from PHDRS in link64.lds.S ensures
only valid non-overlapping load segments are generated.
---
 plat/kvm/x86/link64.lds.S | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/plat/kvm/x86/link64.lds.S b/plat/kvm/x86/link64.lds.S
index fc156a0..5ad621f 100644
--- a/plat/kvm/x86/link64.lds.S
+++ b/plat/kvm/x86/link64.lds.S
@@ -37,8 +37,6 @@ PHDRS
 	text PT_LOAD FLAGS(PHDRS_PF_RX);
 	rodata PT_LOAD FLAGS(PHDRS_PF_R);
 	data PT_LOAD;
-	tls PT_TLS;
-	tls_load PT_LOAD;
 	stack PT_GNU_STACK FLAGS(PHDRS_PF_RW);
 }
 
-- 
